`src/Aether.Atf.Core` is a derivative of SonyWWS ATF `Framework/Atf.Core`
(namespace `Sce.Atf`). `src/Aether.Atf.Commands` is a derivative of the
logic-only command / undo / history / document slice of
`Framework/Atf.Gui`. `src/Aether.Atf.PropertyEditing` is a derivative of
the logic-only property-editing types from `Framework/Atf.Gui`
(`Controls/PropertyEditing` and DOM property-descriptor adapters).
`src/Aether.Atf.DomGen` and `src/Aether.Atf.DomGen.Cli` (`aether-domgen`)
are derivatives of SonyWWS ATF `DevTools/DomGen`. `samples/UsingDom` and
`samples/UsingDom.Document` retarget ATF `Samples/UsingDom` (schema +
document graph) plus property-editing descriptors from
`Aether.Atf.PropertyEditing`. `testdata/atf/UsingDom/ogre-adventure-ii.xml`
is the DomXmlWriter form of that sample document. `src/Aether.Editor` and `src/Aether.Plugins` are new Aether hosting
code; they are not Sony products. Sony and PlayStation names appear only
in About / NOTICE to describe ATF origin. Host plugins use
Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection. ATF Core / Commands /
PropertyEditing still use System.ComponentModel.Composition.
See PORTING.md for the portable subset and cuts.

